.TH GIT-IT 1 "November 23, 2026" "git-it 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-it \- inspect, synchronize, and publish Git repository trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-it
.RI [ options ] " [command]" " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Bash 5+ command for Termux and Linux. Inspection is local. Recursive
operations
follow registered submodules. Completed work is retained after partial
failure.
.PP
With no command, print usage. Outside a worktree also print a warning and
usage to stderr and exit 3. Explicit --help succeeds in any directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show the local repository summary alone.
.TP
.B path
Show the current root, or format verified repository ancestry.
.TP
.B status, -s, --status
Report the selected worktree and registered submodules parent first.
Group changed files by index and worktree state. Show cached tracking counts
and both paths for renames or copies. Missing children make the report
incomplete. Dirty worktrees and ordinary file conflicts are successful reports.
Status does not fetch, initialize children or refresh the index.
.TP
.B sync
Fetch and fast-forward the root upstream, then check out recorded submodule
commits, parent before children. Use --init to initialize missing children.
Safe siblings continue after blockers.
.TP
.B publish
Preview, confirm, commit and push, children before parents. Defaults to staged
changes and successfully published child pointers. Publication needs an owned
destination and an attached, unambiguous upstream. Failed children block
parents.
.TP
.B submodule NAME [ACTION]
Select a registered child by name. Actions include info, status and publish.
.TP
.B submodules [ACTION] [PATH]
Inspect registered descendants, limit the tree with --depth N, or review
publication of one registered path or all direct submodules.
.TP
.B wiki [info|status|sync|publish]
Select the declared Wiki or a sibling checkout with a matching Wiki remote.
An inferred sibling participates in top-level inspection. Select its Wiki
command explicitly for synchronization or publication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-C, --directory " DIR
Working directory.
.TP
.B -i, --icon
Nerd Font host icon, independent of ownership. Empty output outside Git.
.TP
.B -o, --owner
Print the complete remote namespace.
.TP
.B -H, --host
Print the host.
.TP
.B -r, --repo
Print the repository name.
.TP
.B -p, --protocol
Print the transport protocol.
.TP
.B -R, --url
Print the sanitized fetch URL.
.TP
.B --https
Print the HTTPS form of the selected SSH or HTTPS URL. May be combined with
-R. Retains the path, resolves configured SSH host aliases, and drops SSH
ports. Local paths and unsupported transports produce an empty field.
.TP
.B -s, --short, --view default|short|verbose
Select the human status view. The verbose view adds metadata and status codes.
.TP
.B --full-paths
Show absolute paths in human status reports.
.TP
.BI "--remote " NAME
Inspection remote. With sync, --remote takes no argument and advances children
to explicitly configured branches instead of parent-recorded commits.
.TP
.BI "--get " FIELD
Print one uncolored field.
.TP
.B --json
Structured output without ANSI colors.
.TP
.BI "-f, --format " FORMAT
Named {field} placeholders. Double braces produce literal braces. No
evaluation.
.TP
.B --list-fields
List fields without requiring a repository.
.TP
.B -n, --no-newline
Suppress the final inspection newline.
.TP
.B --outermost
Start operations at the outermost verified parent instead of the current repo.
.TP
.B --init
Allow sync to initialize missing registered submodules.
.TP
.B --no-wiki
Exclude the associated Wiki from a top-level command.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Local preview with no network or repository writes. Remote state is unknown.
.TP
.B --all
Publish tracked and untracked changes, respecting ignore rules.
.TP
.BI "-m, --message " MESSAGE
Set the commit message. The default is "Sync via NAME on TIMESTAMP" in UTC.
NAME comes from the DOTS_PROFILE environment variable when set and nonempty,
otherwise from the hostname.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept publication preview. Required for noninteractive publication.
.TP
.BI "--config " FILE
Read Git-config syntax from FILE instead of the XDG config location.
.TP
.B --no-config
Ignore configuration.
.TP
.BI "--color " auto|always|never
Color policy. Auto requires a terminal and an unset NO_COLOR variable.
Each output stream is checked separately. Explicit always overrides NO_COLOR.
Help, summary labels, operation statuses and diagnostics use color.
JSON, single-field values, formatted output, version output and completion
source remain uncolored.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable colors.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Show full operation paths and routine status explanations. Inspection adds
sanitized remote details and verified ancestry. Does not expose raw Git logs.
Repeated flags have no additional effect. JSON, bare path output, field values,
prompt formats, icons, field lists, version output and completion source are
unchanged. There is no verbosity configuration key.
.TP
.B --no-progress
Disable terminal progress for status, sync, and publish.
.TP
.BI "--completion " bash|zsh|fish
Generate completion source without reading a repository.
Zsh identifies commands separately from options and values so shell preferences
can color the menu by type. Inserted tokens remain literal; the completion
does not change global styles or require Dots.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print usage with the current logo.txt header. The installed logo lives at
share/git-it/logo.txt under the selected prefix.
Help requires no Git repository.
.SH HUMAN OUTPUT
Human output follows the active Dots profile when available, including its help
styles, Git and file colors, icons and layout.
Standalone defaults apply elsewhere.
Human info and status abbreviate home paths using a tilde.
Use status --full-paths for literal absolute paths.
Terminal reports open with one blank line. Default info and status show the
root heading and metadata box, followed by consecutive submodule rows. The
last submodule's guide continues to the Wiki when it is displayed. A lone
repository omits the outer guide. Submodule reports name the originally
targeted repository and branch above the selected results.
Status groups files by their complete index and worktree state.
Operations show the root once and relative descendant paths; a dot means the
operation root. Routine successes use one line unless verbose output is enabled.
.PP
Blocker and failure reasons, publication selections and destinations, commit
messages, child-pointer caveats, and dry-run uncertainty are always visible.
Terminal boxes group operation settings, per-repository planning fields and
result explanations. File lists and confirmation prompts appear outside them.
Publication preview and execution have separate headings. Final results identify
completion, incomplete work, previews, and cancellation.
.PP
Inspection describes ownership as a configured owner match, not proof of access.
Absent metadata is displayed as Not configured.
.PP
Status, sync and publish display delayed progress on stderr. A spinner marks
active work and a bar shows progress when a count is known. The display
clears before results and prompts.
Both stdout and stderr must be terminals; TERM must be set and not dumb.
JSON, dry runs and redirected output stay static even with --color always.
The spinner also works in verbose mode. Color controls apply as usual;
--no-color and NO_COLOR leave plain frames. Use --no-progress to disable
animation, including for helpers that draw their own terminal interface.
.SH FIELDS
root, remote, url, https_url, protocol, host, owner, repo, owned, icon,
current, parent,
outermost, parent_dirname, parent_basename, submodule_prefix,
submodule_basename,
cwd_prefix, path_parent, path_outermost, chain_length, chain_repos,
chain_paths,
is_submodule.
.PP
Paths are physical absolute paths unless explicitly relative. Chains are
arrays
in JSON and newline-separated field values. An ordinary repository has an
empty
parent, outermost equal to current, relative paths of a dot, and chain_length
one.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/git-it/config
is read as data. Includes are disabled. CLI options override configuration.
.PP
.nf
[git-it]
    owner = github.com/5nik7
    owner = gitlab.com/team/subgroup
    hostAlias = github-work=github.com
    color = auto
.fi
.PP
Ownership is an exact host/namespace match, not authentication. No account is
assumed when configuration is absent. Publishing checks the effective push
URL.
.SH INSTALLATION
Run bash install.sh with an optional --prefix directory. The default is PREFIX
on Termux, or HOME/.local otherwise. The installer includes the manual and
completion files for all three shells under that prefix:
.TP
.B share/man/man1/git-it.1
Manual page.
.TP
.B share/bash-completion/completions/git-it
Bash completion, loaded through bash-completion or sourced directly.
.TP
.B share/zsh/site-functions/_git-it
Zsh completion. Include this directory on fpath before running compinit.
.TP
.B share/fish/vendor_completions.d/git-it.fish
Fish completion, loaded through the vendor completion path or sourced directly.
.PP
Custom prefixes may require completion search paths and MANPATH configuration.
.PP
The installer and uninstaller accept -v or --verbose to list managed file
actions. Default output shows the prefix and result. Dry runs always list
intended actions; modified-file preservation warnings are always visible.
Shell startup files are not edited. Install and uninstall accept --dry-run,
--color auto|always|never and --no-color. Auto mode honors NO_COLOR.
Uninstall removes unchanged managed files and preserves modified files.
.PP
Dots can run this same program via
.B dots git it
on Termux, Linux and WSL. Its setup includes the plugin when the recorded
submodule is initialized. Run dots files install --component git-it to link
the user-local command, manual and completions to the plugin checkout.
Edits there take effect on the next invocation.
Add --with-source git-it to acquire the recorded revision on a fresh checkout.
The plugin starts in the caller's working directory.
.SH SAFETY
No automatic stash, reset, clean, force-push, or branch selection. Pinned
checkout
may detach submodule HEAD. Hooks and signing configuration remain enabled.
Existing submodule URL overrides are preserved. Changed topology can require
manual Git work. git-it.lock directories guard overlapping git-it operations;
inspect stale locks before manual removal. Ordinary Git does not honor these
locks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: complete, preview, cancellation or empty prompt outside Git.
1: failed/incomplete operation. 2: invalid arguments/configuration.
3: dependency or repository-context error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-submodule (1),
.BR git-push (1)
